# v0.7 grammar test — subset of CMS69 for lexer/parser/AST/validator testing

// ===== Terminologies (valuesets) =====

terminology "Virtual Encounter Class":
- valueset is ``.

terminology "Encounter to Evaluate BMI":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.600.1.1751`.

terminology "Body Mass Index Observations":
- valueset is ``.


// ===== Asserted concepts =====
// `coded from` body; refs in quotes are valueset names.
// type REQUIRED; valuetype 0..* (multiple value views per type).

// Variation A: single valuetype
concept "Virtual Encounters":
- type is Encounter.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Virtual Encounter Class".

// Variation B: multiple valuetypes (the operator's flagship example)
concept "Encounters to Evaluate BMI":
- type is Encounter.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- value type is Period.
- coded from "Encounter to Evaluate BMI".

// Variation C: omitted valuetype — should be lazy-deduced from type's default
//   (validator behavior pending Phase 4)
concept "BMI Observations":
- type is Observation.
- coded from "Body Mass Index Observations".


// ===== Composition-kind concepts (`defined as`) =====
// `defined as` body; refs in quotes are concept names; uses sem-or/sem-and/sem-not.

// Type explicitly declared — refs must agree with the declared type (per v0.7 rules)
concept "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual)":
- type is Encounter.
- defined as
(
   "Encounters to Evaluate BMI"
   sem-and
   sem-not "Virtual Encounters"
).


// ===== Predicate-kind concepts (`definition is`, narrative) =====
// `definition is` body; refs in quotes are concept names; narrative matched against catalog.

// Type declared, valuetype omitted (Variation B' on definition-is)
concept "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual) Performed":
- type is Encounter.
- definition is "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual)" performed.

// Type declared, valuetype omitted; references "Measurement Period" which is
// a runtime parameter (will be unresolved until imports + parameters land)
concept "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual) During MP":
- type is Encounter.
- definition is "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual)" during "Measurement Period".


// ===== Composition over definition-is concepts =====
// Composition over two definition-is concepts.

concept "Qualifying Encounter":
- type is Encounter.
- defined as
(
   "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual) During MP"
   sem-and
   "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual) Performed"
).


// ===== Optional-type variations (testing type-inference rules) =====

// Variation D: composition-kind concept WITHOUT explicit type — should infer
// type from refs (all are Encounters, so type = Encounter)
concept "Qualifying Encounter (no type declared)":
- defined as
(
   "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual) During MP"
   sem-and
   "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual) Performed"
).

// Variation E: definition-is concept WITHOUT explicit type — should infer
// type from the subject ref (the first concept ref in the narrative)
concept "BMI Encounter Performed (no type declared)":
- definition is "BMI Evaluation Encounter (not virtual)" performed.
